//
// Expected: u0e1 — the dual hazard, in one model. The fields disagree
// honestly, so the equivalence query fails on its own and the search is
// distinguishing free positions throughout the run.
//
// While it does, the attacker may install a bundle whose two fields are the
// SAME value, which would make `left` and `right` observably equal. That
// equality is the attacker's own doing and links nothing: unlinkability must
// stay u0. `find_link_witness` refuses an attacker-authored slot, and this is
// the model that keeps that refusal load-bearing now that the search has a
// reason to be filling both fields at once.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	generates n
	generates m
	bundle = CONCAT(n, m)
]

Alice -> Bob: bundle

principal Bob[
	left, right = SPLIT(bundle)?
	_ = HASH(left, right)
]

queries[
	unlinkability? left, right
	equivalence? left, right
]
